# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]   (no dollar/backtick in the text)
register_gate "tests/test_installation_liveness.py" "INSTALLATION LIVENESS GATE: PASS" "installation liveness" "installation liveness / no-billing-without-a-LIVE-link (commercial-completeness): core.installation_account is the installation->account routing MAP but carried NO liveness state -- the uninstall purge (purge_account_working_set_with_authority) and the suspend release (release_account_claims_with_authority) deliberately KEEP the routing row [uninstall keeps it because the append-only ledger is retained + a reinstall re-binds the SAME id; suspend is reversible], only a GDPR erase deletes it. So the platform's liveness read seam list_installation_ids() [a bare SELECT] reported an UNINSTALLED/SUSPENDED installation as if it were still LIVE -- the exact read the no-billing-without-a-live-link gates depend on, so a dead install could look billable and graph freshness would keep it warm. The fix [function-only + one nullable column, contention-free on prod]: [A] core.installation_account.revoked_at [nullable] is STAMPED now() by the uninstall + suspend handlers and CLEARED by reactivate [revoked_at IS NULL == live]; [B] core.installation_is_live[installation_id] is the platform's per-installation liveness read [true iff mapped AND not revoked; an unknown id is NOT live -- fail-closed]; [C] core.list_installation_ids[] enumerates ONLY live installs. Proven end-to-end: a fresh install is live + enumerated -> uninstall makes it NOT live + drops it from the list WHILE KEEPING the routing row [reinstall re-binds the same id + the audit ledger survives] -> reactivate brings it back live; suspend revokes liveness and unsuspend [reactivate] restores it; an unknown id is never live; a re-delivered suspend revokes nothing the second time [idempotent]. content-free [a timestamp on the routing row, no path/name/body]" "installation liveness: an uninstalled or suspended install no longer looks LIVE to the billing-liveness gates or graph freshness [revoked_at stamped on uninstall/suspend, cleared on reinstall/unsuspend]; the routing row is KEPT so a reinstall re-binds the same id and the audit ledger survives; the no-billing-without-a-live-link read seam now reads true liveness" 24
